    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-geospiza-beak-aspect-ratio-d-l-correlation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-geospiza-magnirostris-vs-geospiza-fuliginosa-depth-scaling-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-group-a-geospiza-pure-scaling-collapse-rms-residual> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 54.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py` (overall weighted score: 56.6/100). The v1 script implements pure diagonal scaling (s_L, s_D) for the 6 Group A Geospiza species (RMS = 0.0040), but omits the full 3-parameter Campas-Brenner affine scaling-and-shear transformation M(s_L, s_D, gamma) needed to collapse all 14 Darwin's finch species across Groups A, B, and C, omits Abzhanov et al.'s (2004, 2006) RCAS::Bmp4, RCAS::Noggin, and RCAS::CaM perturbations and pure-scaling negative control, and does not segment the vendored 1845 Gould Darwin's finches specimen image. Overall 54.8/100 (faithfulness 48.3, reproducibility 70.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 33e07ad; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 36, Parameter expressivity 48, Morphometric validation 56, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py at 33e07ad, image/png, 197687 B, 1560×1105 px, artifact_sha256 777aca548970785f1b2714e16a896382627d991abc3020061ca0d810886d63ee (sha256 777aca548970785f1b2714e16a896382627d991abc3020061ca0d810886d63ee), spec_fingerprint c3ac286b6e1240143c8b941b9ff61a0744669a4b95cb14db7918d73b5259a735. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c3ac286b6e1240143c8b941b9ff61a0744669a4b95cb14db7918d73b5259a735; artifact_sha256: 777aca548970785f1b2714e16a896382627d991abc3020061ca0d810886d63ee; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_reference.json=cf6430de0c52d725..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/darwin_finches_specimen.jpg=5ea7ada14a01ba77..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/paper_citations.bib=f0b9fb929ffd2d09..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/scout_manifest.json=4b321120fd7b2736...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add runtime SHA-256 verification of all 4 files in `datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/`, expose CLI parameter overrides (`--bmp4-scale`, `--cam-scale`, `--gamma-shear`, `--seed`), and expand `self_test()` and `measure_morphoeval()`.",
        "remediation needed: Implement computer-vision contour segmentation on `datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/darwin_finches_specimen.jpg` (Gould's 1845 Darwin's finches lithograph) to extract upper culmen profiles, aspect ratios D/L, and affine collapse residuals across the 4 illustrated finch species.",
        "remediation needed: Implement the 2D/3D Bmp4-Calmodulin mesenchymal growth field, cantilever beam bending mechanics I_beam = W*D^3/(12*L), and Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) retroviral perturbation suite (RCAS::Bmp4, RCAS::Noggin, RCAS::CaM).",
        "remediation needed: Implement the full 3-parameter Campas-Brenner affine scaling-and-shear group M(s_L, s_D, gamma) = [[1, gamma], [0, 1]] @ [[s_L, 0], [0, s_D]] across all 14 Darwin's finch species (Groups A, B, and C), demonstrating both the 6-species Group A pure-scaling collapse and the 14-species universal scaling+shear collapse (RMS < 0.015, r > 0.99) contrasted against the pure-scaling (gamma = 0) negative control on Certhidea and Camarhynchus." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.48e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
